Author: Trang Doan <44855874+trangdoan982@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 16:52:28 2026 -0400

    ENG-2261 Add conflict resolution step to the Obsidian schema import modal (#1444)

    * ENG-2261 Add conflict resolution step to the schema import modal

    Per-field opt-in for items the vault already has. Every checkbox starts
    unchecked, so import never silently clobbers local schema.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

    * ENG-2261 Discard field choices when leaving the conflict step

    Back only changed the step, so re-entering showed prior choices even
    though the step states every field starts on the local value.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

    * ENG-2261 Follow a chosen template body into its renamed copy

    Both sides naming the same template yields no `template` change row, so
    the selected-fields guard never fired and the node type stayed pointed at
    the local file while the copy sat orphaned beside it.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

    * ENG-2261 Name only the template copies the import will actually write

    The footnote listed every template conflict, but one left on the local
    value produces no copy. Also count template body size in real bytes
    rather than UTF-16 code units.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

    ---------

    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

